For those of you who don't want to know it here is a *SPOILER ALERT*



Praying is useful when you are in a desperate situation because your god might
help you (this depends on how desperate the situation is: praying while only
hungry doesn't work but praying when fainting from the lack of food will always
fill your stomach). If there is no trouble around and you are in good standing
with your god praying might give you some kind of blessing. But beware: between
two prayers there is a prayer timeout period of about 800 turns (complicated
formula, varies from 300 to 1500 turns). Sacrifying things to your god helps to
shorten this timeout or mollify them when they got angry after too many prayers.

Selling things is easy. Just drop them inside the shop. The shopkeeper will tell
you how much money he gives you. But if you want the item back you have to buy it
from him.

Throwing rings down sinks gives you some funny messages which help you to
determine what rings you have. There is a tiny (5%) chance of not loosing the
ring.
If you are at it just try engraving with an unknown wand and watch what the bugs
on the floor are doing.

Banks? What banks? Have you been playing too much Larn recently?
If you are talking of the famous chambers full of gold on some levels there is
always a teleporter around that sets you into the chambers. But beware of the
guards! You will know what I mean if you first enter one.

